%I A080839 #38 Nov 12 2026 22:25:22
%S A080839 1,1,1,2,6,27,180,1786,26094,559127,17535396,804131875,53833201737,
%T A080839 5256046698145
%N A080839 Number of positive increasing integer sequences of length n with Gilbreath transform (that is, the diagonal of leading successive absolute differences) given by {1,1,1,1,1,...}.
%C A080839 From _T. D. Noe_, Feb 05 2007: (Start)
%C A080839 The slowest-growing sequence of length n is 1,2,4,6,...,2(n-1). The fastest-growing sequence is 1,2,4,8,...,2^(n-1).
%C A080839 The ratio a(n+1)*a(n-1)/a(n)^2 appears to converge to a constant near 1.46, which is the approximate growth rate of A001609. Are the sequences related? (End)
%C A080839 Also, a(n) is the number of (not necessarily increasing) positive integer sequences of length n-1 with Gilbreath transform (1, ..., 1). - _Pontus von Brömssen_, May 13 2023
%C A080839 With a(14), the ratio a(n+1)*a(n-1)/a(n)^2 continues to decrease: 1.4666, 1.4636, 1.4622, 1.4599, 1.4584 for n = 9..13 (empirical observation). - _Roberto Vetere_, Nov 06 2026
%H A080839 Leila Muney, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.23721">Holes in Valid-Extension Sets of Finite Gilbreath Sequences</a>, arXiv:2606.23721 [math.CO], 2026. See p. 28 (Sect. 14.1).
%H A080839 Roberto Vetere, <a href="https://github.com/RobertoVetere/oeis-a080839">Code and verification for a(14)</a>, GitHub, 2026.
%H A080839 <a href="/index/Ge#Gilbreath">Index entries for sequences related to Gilbreath conjecture and transform</a>.
%e A080839 The table below shows that {1,2,4,6,10} is one of the 6 sequences of length 5 that satisfy the stated condition:
%e A080839    1
%e A080839    2 1
%e A080839    4 2 1
%e A080839    6 2 0 1
%e A080839   10 4 2 2 1
%o A080839 (Python)
%o A080839 from collections import Counter
%o A080839 from itertools import product
%o A080839 def a(n):  # column-wise transfer; state = column of the difference triangle without its top entry
%o A080839     L = Counter({(1,)*(n-1): 1})
%o A080839     for m in range(n-1, 0, -1):
%o A080839         M = Counter()
%o A080839         for s, c in L.items():
%o A080839             if s[0] > 0:
%o A080839                 for t in product(*[(x+y,)+((x-y,) if 0<y<=x else ()) for x, y in zip(s, s[1:])]):
%o A080839                     if m == 1 or t[0] > 0: M[t] += c
%o A080839         L = M
%o A080839     return sum(L.values())
%o A080839 print([a(n) for n in range(1, 12)])  # _Roberto Vetere_, Nov 06 2026
%Y A080839 Cf. A001609, A036262, A363002, A363003, A363004, A363005.
%Y A080839 Cf. also A136465, the total number of increasing sequences with the same maximum length. [From _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Aug 08 2010]
%K A080839 nonn,more,changed
%O A080839 1,4
%A A080839 _John W. Layman_, Mar 28 2003
%E A080839 More terms from _T. D. Noe_, Feb 05 2007
%E A080839 Added "positive" to definition. - _N. J. A. Sloane_, May 13 2023
%E A080839 a(14) from _Roberto Vetere_, Nov 06 2026
